SELECT 12, 53, 7, 1.00, N'What is the central premise asserted by the author regarding modern attention spans?', N'In an era characterized by hyper-connectivity and pervasive notification streams, deep contemplation has become a scarce cognitive commodity. The human attention mechanism is continually fragmented by algorithmic feedback loops tailored to stimulate dopamine responses. Renowned cognitive theorists argue that this persistent cognitive interruption induces neuroplastic adaptations that favor superficial skimming over sustained analytical deduction. To preserve high-order conceptual thinking, knowledge workers must cultivate deliberate practices of monastic focus and cognitive sanctuary, disengaging periodically from ubiquitous digital stimuli.', N'Tác giả khẳng định luồng thông báo liên tục và vòng lặp thuật toán khiến khả năng chú ý bị phân mảnh, ưu tiên đọc lướt hời hợt hơn tư duy phân tích sâu.', NULL, N'TracNghiem', N'Doc', N'Kho', N'[{"MaLuaChon":212,"KyHieuLuaChon":"A","NoiDungLuaChon":"Human memory storage capacity has doubled in the digital age.","LaDapAnDung":false},{"MaLuaChon":213,"KyHieuLuaChon":"B","NoiDungLuaChon":"Algorithmic interruptions promote superficial skimming at the expense of deep deduction.","LaDapAnDung":true},{"MaLuaChon":214,"KyHieuLuaChon":"C","NoiDungLuaChon":"Social media notifications permanently cure workplace anxiety.","LaDapAnDung":false},{"MaLuaChon":215,"KyHieuLuaChon":"D","NoiDungLuaChon":"Multitasking is proven to enhance complex philosophical reasoning.","LaDapAnDung":false}]'
UNION ALL
